{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China has weaponized its critical minerals\nmonopoly, on which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4120,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the entire Western industrial base\ndepends."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8080,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to the European Council\nof Foreign Relations experts, Doctor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11720,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tobias Gherke,\nThis dependency is even worse"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15120,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than Europe's\n2021 dependance on Russian gas,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18200,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which led to a massive energy\ncrisis in 2022."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22200,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if China cuts its critical minerals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24840,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "completely today,\nour industry is not prepared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28320,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Vast elements of our base industry\nin Europe, but also in other places,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33360,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rely on these UN access\nto permanent magnets, most importantly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37320,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if that would stop tomorrow,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40720,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quite frankly, some of these industries,\nlike the automotive industry,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44040,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would grind to a halt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45560,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There would be no more production\nvery quickly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48600,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that would have incredible\ncascading effects."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52320,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine that 13 million people are\nemployed in the car industry in Europe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56080,
    "dDurationMs": 640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58040,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "95% of them would stop production."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60840,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, we are talking,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63400,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an economic crisis\nof historic proportions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65800,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No wonder governments ranging from Europe\nto the US to India, are scrambling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70240,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to reduce their dependance\non Chinese minerals like rare earths,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74280,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "copper and lithium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76320,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this will be incredibly hard."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80080,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China's mineral monopoly is protected\nby its massive scale,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83880,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "massive government subsidies,\nlax environmental regulations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87800,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and China churns out \nhundreds of thousands"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91680,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of academics\nand PhDs in mining and geology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96120,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, you know, in Europe,\nit's a drop in the ocean."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99640,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so, even if you're now wouldn’t\nwant to reverse this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103440,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know that, \nthe deck is stacked against us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108040,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there is hope for the West\nin the 1980s and 1990s, the West"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112120,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dominated all of these industries,\nand China was able to break"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115520,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through the Western monopoly\nthrough clever policies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118800,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So can the West learn from China\nto take back its sovereignty?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122880,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, absolutely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124320,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this video, I'll show you how\nthey can do it in five steps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127920,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But before getting into the specifics,\nlet's do a quick recap"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131240,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of why critical minerals are so important."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135440,
    "dDurationMs": 760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For simplicity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136200,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's start with the critical minerals\nthat have been in the news the most."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140280,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We are discussing, \ncritical minerals and rare earths."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144400,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Probably heard people\ntalking recently about rare,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146880,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what is so special\nabout these rare earths?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149960,
    "dDurationMs": 400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150360,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The F-35 jet, state of the art US\nNavy destroyer nuclear attack submarines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155320,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I found they all contain\nthousands of pounds of rare earths."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159400,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what for the main product\nthat is made out of refined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164160,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rare earths is our permanent magnets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166960,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are magnets\nthat do not need an external power source"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170520,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to generate their magnetic field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172720,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They allow modern wind turbines,\nfor example,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175400,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to transform wind into electricity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177880,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are at the core of loudspeakers,\nmicrophones, and all of our headphones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183240,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The new Nintendo Switch to has super"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185880,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "snappy\nmagnetic attachments that sound like this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190880,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sounds good, but perhaps more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192360,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crucially, modern cars\ncannot be made without permanent magnets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196520,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They power your car's trunk sense\nor your car's steering system, its air"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200480,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "conditioning actuator, the window\nlifting motor and for electric vehicles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204840,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even its entire motor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206320,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is why it really matters to that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209160,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China holds holds a global share of earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213240,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "refining and permanent magnet production,\nsomewhere around 95%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217280,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And worryingly,\nChina has recently introduced"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219720,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a licensing system\nthat requires any firm in the world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223200,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to apply for a Chinese license\nto use these magnets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228120,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And need to go to Beijing and say, hello,\nI'm Volkswagen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231960,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I need that permanent magnet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233560,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do I get a license if Beijing says no?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236320,
    "dDurationMs": 680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Volkswagen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237000,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stellantis for the entire western\ncar industry ground to a halt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241800,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And even if they can replace\nall the permanent magnets all over Western"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cars, that will be so expensive\nthat they would soon be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248400,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crushed by competitors\nthat do have a license from Beijing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252360,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China has already shown\nthat it is willing to use economic weapons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255600,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like this to devastate local industries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258720,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, in 2023, China no longer\ngranted Chinese firms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262440,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "licenses to export graphite to Sweden."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265440,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It wasn't exactly clear\nwhy it did this, but publications"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268480,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like The Economist have mentioned\nthat it may have been triggered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271520,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when a Swedish free speech group\ngave an award to a Chinese dissident."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276520,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Although the reason could also\nhave been strategic for a while,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279520,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sweden's promising battery startup\nNorthvolt seemed like the only company"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284440,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that could be competitive\nagainst Chinese producers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288000,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But two years after China's ban,\nSweden's Northvolt"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292000,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shut its doors for good in Sweden"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294880,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only 10 to 15 years ago,\nthis would be unthinkable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298440,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Back then, the dominant idea"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299760,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was that the global free market\njust determines everything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302960,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If a battery company wants to buy minerals\nand it is in short supply,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306640,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the price will just go up for everyone\nat the same time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309720,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the highest bidder, well,\nthey will buy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312480,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only job of the government\nwas still at the free market."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315120,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Function as efficiently as possible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317680,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This logic no longer works today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320200,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Governments are increasingly realizing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322600,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their role is no longer\njust about making markets efficient."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326200,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's also about protecting domestic\nindustries from foreign manipulation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330440,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, governments have now\nbeen forced to think carefully about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "critical minerals and critical materials\nmore broadly, which are defined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338520,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as any materials that have, number one,\na high risk of supply chain disruption."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343800,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And number two, serve an essential\nfunction in one or more technologies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348120,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By this definition, a rare\nearths are clearly a critical material."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353000,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China now has a massive power\nover foreign manufacturing firms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356480,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it has a monopoly\nor near monopoly in the two"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360280,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other parts of the supply chain\nmining and refining."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364320,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On average,\nChina controls 54% of rare earth mining."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But far more importantly, it controls\nabout 77% of rare earth refining."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374120,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the pattern that we see\nall across industries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377040,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that power the modern,\nincreasingly electrified global economy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380720,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, if we look at copper,\nwhich is the main conductor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383560,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of electricity, we can see that\nmining is relatively diversified."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388040,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even though Chile, the Congo\nand Peru are the biggest producers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392360,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when it comes to refining,\nChina is much more dominant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396560,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the West's critical material\nvulnerability is not purely limited"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400040,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to China."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400920,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Think, for example, nickel,\nwhich is a key input in steel production,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404280,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it is one of the most promising metals\nto be used in batteries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408240,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, supply is not secure at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410560,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Given that Indonesia is the epicenter\nof global nickel production"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413680,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and now also refining what you see,\nlike China,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418000,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Indonesia has shown that it is more\nthan willing to use its nickel dominance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421680,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as an economic weapon, as it has banned\nall raw nickel exports"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425800,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to ensure that it also dominates\nthe nickel refinement industry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429960,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, so far,\nChina has smartly moved in to make sure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433480,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "many of the best Indonesian based\nnickel refineries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436560,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are in fact Chinese companies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439040,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But nickel is a rare exception where\na country other than China dominates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443160,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you look at the most common\nelement used in batteries,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445760,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lithium, we can again see that in mining."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448880,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sure, China is a big player,\nbut Australia is actually more important."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453160,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, Australian mines largely\ndepend on Chinese refining capacity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458040,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making Western battery manufacturers again\nlargely dependent on China."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463160,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This pattern holds for almost all critical\nminerals graphite, cobalt, you name it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468360,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mining\ndominance is different for a mineral,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470800,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even if China\nalmost always plays a big role."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473360,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the real story is about refinery."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475920,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China dominates\nalmost all critical mineral"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478520,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "refinery, giving it an insanely powerful\neconomic weapon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481720,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it is\nnow starting to use to get both Western"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483960,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and non-Western countries\nlike India to do what it wants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487280,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But before we get to\nhow the West can respond, this, of course,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491000,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "raises the question why is China\nso dominant in mineral refinement?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496160,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because it really wasn't always like this\njust a few decades ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499920,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, after the Second World War,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501640,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the dominant rare earth player\nwas actually the United States"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505440,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thanks to the massive mountain\npass mines in California."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509240,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, ironically, as US Treasury\nSecretary Scott Bessent recently said,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514080,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the technology, especially in rare earth\nmagnets, it's being used against us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518640,
    "dDurationMs": 600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519240,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "technology, but Japan and Europe\nalso played a major role."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522840,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "France, Germany, Portugal, Spain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of them had strong\nmineral mining industries and not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531160,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what happened?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 532240,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How did the Chinese take over this\nstrategic industry?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536280,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The answer actually consists of two parts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539400,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first part is Chinese strategy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542280,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Interestingly, there are some rumors\nthat China's rare earth monopoly was a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546120,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "result of a grand geo economic strategy\nset out already by Deng Xiapeng in 1992."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552360,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But according to Michaela Roibu."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554520,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I hope I pronounced correctly\nwho was doing her doctoral research"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557880,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on China's rare earth monopoly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559440,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China's current\ndominance is probably and ironically,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562200,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a result of industrial protection by Japan\nand the US in the 1990s, which excluded"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567480,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chinese firms from obtaining\nthe know how to refine critical minerals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572280,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now to counter this,\nthey were forced to attract a lot of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576280,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "foreign investment and talent\nand knowhow into minerals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580360,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and to the mineral space,\nmostly from Europe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582960,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they did this by giving foreigners\nall sorts of juicy advantages,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587400,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like tax credits\nthat gave lax environmental protection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591200,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Crucially, the Europeans\nlet them do this. Why?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594520,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, two reasons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595560,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first is the increasingly dominant\nfree market philosophy in the 1990s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600400,
    "dDurationMs": 920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If European firms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601320,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could produce more cheaply in China,\nthen of course they were free to do it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605160,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second reason\nwas environmental protection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607320,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see, refining critical minerals\nis really a really dirty business."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612880,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You will need a lot of a big chemical mix"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615480,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to clean, to wash off the actual mineral\nthat you want."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 619200,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The 1990s was also a time of rising\nenvironmental regulations in the West."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623560,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Western firms could dodge\nthese regulations by moving to China."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627120,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And politicians were actually quite happy\nto be rid of these highly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630760,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "polluting industries. Bye bye."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633520,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, just as with Western car firms\nmoving to China,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636480,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Chinese had regulations in place\nthat all foreign firms needed to set up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640760,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "local joint ventures where they had\nto transfer knowledge to China"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645040,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if they wanted to work cheaply in China."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648840,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The thing is, businesses care\nabout profits in the next couple of years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652680,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They do not strategize about competition\nin 40 years time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657120,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they happily moved their production\nto China."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659280,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But today, after 3 or 4 decades,\njust as German car manufacturers now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 663360,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "struggle to compete with the Chinese\nfirms, the rare earth mining"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666640,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and especially refinery business\nis now dominated by Chinese firms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 671240,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "giving the Chinese government\ntheir incredibly powerful economic weapon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675320,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, of course, Western governments\nare now struggling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678040,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to respond and actually,\nit may be too late."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681800,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For at least four reasons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684960,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Environmental regulations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686840,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is, number one, are still much\nstricter in the West than in China."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691000,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Reason number two Chinese firms now\nhave massive, massive scale advantages."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696440,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Reason number three Chinese firms\nin strategic sectors are often"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700160,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heavily subsidized by the government\nif they need it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704440,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then finally, number four,\nChina churns out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707920,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hundreds of thousands of academics\nand PhDs in mining and geology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713400,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, you know, in Europe\nit's a drop in the ocean."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716920,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so even if you and I wouldn't\nwant to reverse this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720720,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know, that the, \nthe deck is stacked against us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725360,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet the deck was also stacked\nagainst China in the 1990s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when all of the knowhow\nand technology was in the West."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732720,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what can the West learn from China?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734640,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's how the West should respond."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737320,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And actually,\nthis is not just applicable to the West."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740240,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's applicable to any country\nthat wants to remain independent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743400,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the new age of geo economics, where\ngreat powers, including those in the West,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747720,
    "dDurationMs": 920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I have to say,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 748640,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will not hesitate to use economic weapons\nto achieve political goals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753440,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Any country that wants sovereignty in this\nage needs a grand geo economic strategy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758840,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in which they set themselves a goal\nfor how independent they want to be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763400,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Importantly, such a strategy\nis not just about critical minerals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766680,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It considers minerals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768000,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It considers oil."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769080,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It considers cloud\ncomputing infrastructure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772000,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It considers an entire economy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774560,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Having a ground geo\neconomic strategy does not mean"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777200,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every country\nshould be independent in everything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780240,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Giving it complete\nindependence is often simply impossible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784320,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in all cases extremely inefficient."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787120,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So any Western strategy should focus\non achieving the right balance between"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791440,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "full free market type specialization\nand autarky for critical minerals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796360,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means the following step number one\nis that Western governments should learn"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800080,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from China who is, by the way, already\nstockpiling oil, grain and even pork."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804080,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, in the age of geo economics,\nevery nation needs some buffers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808280,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case of critical minerals,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 810320,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the most part, Western governments\nare already starting to do this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813800,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or planning to do this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 815840,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Step number two."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817120,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most Western governments need to realize\nthat gaining some more independence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 820440,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from Chinese minerals can best be done\nin a big alliance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824280,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Europe and Japan\ndon't have many minerals, but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827240,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they do have some knowhow left\nand they have lots of money to invest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831480,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Australia and Canada\nhave lots of minerals,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833360,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they almost completely rely on Chinese\nrefineries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837000,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, Western governments\nlike Japan, Australia, Canada and EU,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840720,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the US and Australia\nand many more are already forming"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844440,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mineral alliances\nbetween individual countries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 847720,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in my opinion,\nthese individual alliances are likely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850680,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much less effective than a concerted\nbig group effort."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854560,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just as NATO as a big alliance\nis far more effective than a patchwork"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857960,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of defensive alliances\nbetween individual states, and Mineral"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861320,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alliance is also far more effective\nif it is big."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 864120,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Still, even with a big, very big alliance,\nstep number three is needed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 868320,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We know that Chinese industrial advantages\nare now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 871680,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just too big for private Western companies\nto overcome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875240,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On top of that,\nas Scott Bessent recently said,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 878080,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any time anyone tries to stand up\none of these rare earths"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881760,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "critical mineral facilities, Chinese\ncome in, they flood the market."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885680,
    "dDurationMs": 680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 886360,
    "dDurationMs": 760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Chinese state"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887120,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is actively coordinating its industry to\nprevent foreign competition from rising."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 892000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, a free market approach\njust will not work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 895320,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, governments need to study and\ncopy China's industrial policy approach."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 899600,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a group, they should use\nindustrial policy tools like subsidies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902960,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "price floors and tariffs to help\nthe mineral, mining and, crucially,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 907320,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "refinery industries\nrecover in allied countries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On top of that, in step number four,\nWestern countries should use industrial"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914760,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "policy tools like subsidies and tariffs\nstrategically to speed up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 918960,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the development of alternative\nand recycling technologies as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 923200,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yes, this is already happening."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925920,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, France is building a massive\nmagnet recycling plant in the south."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930680,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when it comes\nto technological replacement,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933560,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "BMW, BMV and Renault\nare already experimenting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937400,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the new electric motors\nthat do not rely on rare earths."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941240,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But these are just small initiatives."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 943480,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is no big strategic effort yet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946640,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The potential of Chinese retaliation\nthen brings us to step five."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950760,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Western countries\nshould develop a portfolio"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952600,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of other technologies and materials\non which China relies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955680,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they should create a doctrine\nthat determines what happens"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 959080,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if any ally faces a geo economic attack."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 962040,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because even mineral poor regions\nlike Europe are not powerless."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 967200,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine Europe would say, in response\nto China threatening"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970440,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to cut roads in\nEurope would respond and say,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974160,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then we will cut off the maintenance\nand servicing of Airbus aircraft in China."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979360,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would be huge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 980920,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly,\nlike Russia did in 2020, China holds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983840,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "almost all of its financial reserves\nin Western currencies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 987280,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in this step five, it's clear\nthat there is enough leverage in the West"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 991480,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make a doctrine that essentially makes\nclear in geoeconomic terms that if you do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 996360,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "X, I will do y, and our\ny needs to be very large and painful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1001600,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because you want to escalate\nin order to de-escalate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004640,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And while, of course, it is clear"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1005960,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that when it comes to critical minerals,\nthese five steps are intended to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1009080,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "counter China."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010280,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I personally think Western countries\nshould develop their geo economic strategy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1014560,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not just to target critical minerals,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1017160,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and also not just to target China."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020440,
    "dDurationMs": 920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have to be honest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1021360,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China is not unique in using geo"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023200,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economic weapons\nto get others to do what they want."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026240,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Under Trump, the US is doing this as well,\nand as we've seen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1030400,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "throughout history, the West has done\nthis from time to time as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1034160,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But yeah, that's my take.\nHave I been unfair to China?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1036680,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do these steps make any sense?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038880,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Am I forgetting something?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040080,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let me know in the comments below\nand if you are interested in in-depth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1044080,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "follow up analysis, I highly recommend\nyou check out our advertising sponsor,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1048520,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Economist, specifically, I recommend\nyou check out this, detailed analysis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1053080,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about how China's licensing system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1055160,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is actually using America's\nown trade weapons to beat it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1059160,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then follow up with this analysis\nabout why China's power over"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1062280,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rare earths may not be as great\nas it seems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1065480,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, how all of this\nso far means that arguably,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069200,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "China is winning the trade war."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071760,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This kind of detailed, balanced analysis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1074280,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are exactly why I highly recommend\nyou subscribe to The Economist,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1078440,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which now offers an exclusive 35% discount\nfor Money Macro viewers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083920,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whether you prefer their app, podcasts\nand newsletters, or whether you are like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1087520,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "me and prefer to catch up on the global\neconomy during the weekend,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1091400,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sitting down with a nice cup of coffee\nand the paper edition."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1095160,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You'll always stay on top of the latest\nglobal developments,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1098240,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no matter where you are.\nSo don't miss out!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1101320,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Click the link in the description\nor top comment below, or head over"
    } ]
  }, {
